WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.212
We begin with lists, which store multiple values in order.

00:00:04.212 --> 00:00:09.392
Then we use indexes and slices to retrieve specific parts of a list.

00:00:09.392 --> 00:00:15.622
Next, we modify lists, loop through them, and summarize numeric values.

00:00:15.622 --> 00:00:21.659
After that, tuples give us a similar ordered structure that is intended to stay fixed.

00:00:22.455 --> 00:00:27.837
By the end, you should be able to look at a data task and decide whether you need a flexible list or a fixed

00:00:27.837 --> 00:00:29.340
tuple.
